From: Spot OCS2 Humble compatibility layer
Subject: [PATCH] Exclude unused perceptive ANYmal examples

The Spot controller does not use the perceptive ANYmal demos. They require
plane-segmentation packages from elevation_mapping_cupy, so exclude the
subtree from colcon discovery rather than carrying that unrelated repository.

diff --git a/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_perceptive_anymal/COLCON_IGNORE b/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_perceptive_anymal/COLCON_IGNORE
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ocs2_robotic_examples/ocs2_perceptive_anymal/COLCON_IGNORE
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+The Spot controller does not build the perceptive ANYmal examples.
+Those examples require elevation_mapping_cupy plane-segmentation packages.
